  "limitations": [
    "The API uses synchronous File I/O and must run on a dedicated storage thread or bounded blocking executor.",
    "Process-local normalized-path and Unix inode guards prevent local duplicate writers. Cross-process exclusive ownership remains the caller contract; this is not an operating-system file lock.",
    "Successful append uses File::sync_data; open/recovery syncs accepted data and the resolved parent directory. The configured filesystem must support directory synchronization.",
    "Synthetic I/O faults, torn-prefix files and child-process exit without destructors do not qualify physical power loss, storage hardware flush behavior, network filesystems or Windows.",
    "A complete entry whose append sync failed may reappear after reopening. That append outcome is ambiguous; recovery synchronizes accepted bytes before success.",
    "A partial file header fails closed. Tail inspection conservatively refuses repair if opaque torn payload bytes happen to contain a checksum-valid later-offset entry header.",
    "Checksums detect corruption but do not authenticate hostile rewriting. Paths are trusted configuration. External mutation is unsupported; observed growth/integrity changes fail closed.",
    "Unsigned64-bit logical offsets and opaque payload record counts do not validate Kafka signed offsets or record batches. No replication, transaction durability, retention or production broker qualification is claimed.",
    "The standalone broker remains publish=false and adds no dependencies/default features to the client."
  ],
